# {{ project_slug }}

Target Python >= {{ python_version }}. Application code belongs in
`src/{{ project_slug }}/`; tests belong in `tests/`.

Use uv for dependencies and the version required by `uv.toml`. Create `uv.lock`
once after generation, then commit it. Use locked installs and commands for
validation. Update dependencies and their lockfile together intentionally.

Tasks are defined in `scripts/app.toml`. Run `uv run --locked poe validate`
before completing a change. This checks committed code without fixing it.
For local repairs, `uv run --locked poe flc` fixes lint, formats, and checks types.
Install commit hooks with `uv run --locked poe install-hooks`.

Strict mypy covers both source and tests. Add annotations and available dependency
stubs; scope unavoidable untyped-import exceptions to specific dependencies.

Use pytest fixtures and isolated temporary directories. Keep installed-package
imports working without injecting `src` into PYTHONPATH. Test public behavior
and regression cases. `poe test-cov` reports branch coverage; choose meaningful
coverage requirements for the application.
{% if include_docker %}

For packaging or startup changes, build and run the Docker image. Keep metadata
and runtime assets available during packaging, select runtime extras explicitly,
and preserve the non-root runtime user.
{% endif %}
